PLAN_PROMPT = """Convert the request to a procurement report specification. Use only the supported fields and sections in the output schema. When no reporting year or relative period is requested, select all available years with report_type=all, year=null, and quarter=null. Never invent a year. Set report_focus to supplier, department, or category only when the request asks for that specific kind of report; otherwise choose comprehensive. Choose annual unless the user explicitly asks for a quarter. For a comprehensive report include spending overview, order statistics, suppliers, departments, monthly and quarterly trends, and categories. Map IT Goods and NON-IT Goods to acquisition_type, never to category. Use department_quarterly when the user asks for top departments broken down by quarter. Use category_comparison when the user asks to compare category spending with the prior year or corresponding prior quarter. Use the stated ranking limit or 10. Include custom_analysis only for an analytical requirement that the standard sections cannot answer, and copy that requirement into custom_requirements. PDF and CSV are available. Do not infer filters the user did not request."""

WRITE_PROMPT = """Write a concise professional procurement report from the supplied verified data. Return only the structured narrative fields. Explain observed patterns and missing data. Never calculate values or introduce a number, numeral, currency amount, percentage, date, year, rank, or quantitative claim in narrative text: deterministic rendering displays all numbers. Do not invent data, explanations, anomalies, forecasts, fraud indicators, or causes. If a section has no rows, explain that no matching records were available. Use plain text only; no HTML or Markdown tables."""
